WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.267
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:10.267
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:16.238
Unit nineteen: Writing a Short Report. Today you will organise and write a clear short report.

4
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:19.167
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.598
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.439
Report.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.123
Report means a formal document with findings.

8
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:31.159
Write a short report.

9
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.321
Your turn. Say: Report.

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.168
Report.

11
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:39.999
Abstract.

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.563
Abstract means a short summary at the start.

13
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.453
Read the abstract.

14
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.400
Your turn. Say: Abstract.

15
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.279
Abstract.

16
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:53.878
Method.

17
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:56.848
Method means how research was done.

18
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.869
Describe the method.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.683
Your turn. Say: Method.

20
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:05.407
Method.

21
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.244
Findings.

22
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.284
Findings means what was discovered.

23
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:12.268
Present the findings.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.466
Your turn. Say: Findings.

25
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.348
Findings.

26
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:21.317
Recommendation.

27
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:24.792
Recommendation means advice for action.

28
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:26.918
Make a recommendation.

29
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:30.134
Your turn. Say: Recommendation.

30
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.326
Recommendation.

31
00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:36.015
Survey.

32
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:39.678
Survey means a set of questions to many people.

33
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:41.470
We ran a survey.

34
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:44.422
Your turn. Say: Survey.

35
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.233
Survey.

36
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:50.042
Respondent.

37
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.827
Respondent means a person who answers a survey.

38
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:56.126
Ten respondents agreed.

39
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:59.857
Your turn. Say: Respondent.

40
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.852
Respondent.

41
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:05.711
Appendix.

42
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:09.355
Appendix means extra material at the end.

43
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.369
See the appendix.

44
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:14.810
Your turn. Say: Appendix.

45
00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:18.575
Appendix.

46
00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:22.959
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:26.025
Visal, what is in a short report?

48
00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:38.732
A report has a title, an abstract, an introduction, the method, the findings, a conclusion and recommendations. Each part has a heading.

49
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:41.735
Which tense do I use?

50
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:54.323
Use the past simple for the method and findings, such as we surveyed fifty students, and the present simple for general facts and recommendations.

51
00:02:55.417 --> 00:02:57.068
How do I present results?

52
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:10.902
Use short sentences, numbers and a table or chart. State the main finding first, then give details, for example sixty percent of respondents preferred online lessons.

53
00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:14.194
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.663
Grammar focus: Past simple for method and findings.

55
00:03:18.963 --> 00:03:20.069
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.841
We surveyed fifty students.

57
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.435
Sixty percent preferred online lessons.

58
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:35.509
Describe the method and findings in the past simple. Use the present simple for recommendations, such as The school should offer more online lessons.

59
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.632
Be careful! Don't say: We survey fifty students.

60
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:45.391
Say: We surveyed fifty students.

61
00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.574
Use past simple for method.

62
00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.961
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.186
A Student Survey.

64
00:03:53.486 --> 00:03:56.112
Ratana writes a report on study habits.

65
00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.052
She surveyed fifty students about online lessons.

66
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:04.448
Sixty percent of respondents preferred online classes.

67
00:04:05.433 --> 00:04:07.920
She presents the findings in a clear table.

68
00:04:08.933 --> 00:04:11.873
She recommends more flexible lessons for students.

69
00:04:12.967 --> 00:04:17.177
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:18.017 --> 00:04:20.016
An abstract is a short blank.

71
00:04:20.316 --> 00:04:23.354
A, menu. B, summary. C, map.

72
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.039
The answer is B: summary.

73
00:04:30.183 --> 00:04:32.740
The method describes how research was blank.

74
00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.171
A, lost. B, sold. C, done.

75
00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:41.396
The answer is C: done.

76
00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.561
A respondent answers a blank.

77
00:04:44.861 --> 00:04:48.224
A, survey. B, door. C, song.

78
00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.511
The answer is A: survey.

79
00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.290
Findings use the past blank.

80
00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:00.034
A, base. B, simple. C, future.

81
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.356
The answer is B: simple.

82
00:05:06.517 --> 00:05:08.748
How many students did Ratana survey?

83
00:05:09.048 --> 00:05:12.934
A, five. B, five hundred. C, fifty.

84
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.813
The answer is C: fifty.

85
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.175
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:24.017 --> 00:05:25.621
What is in a short report?

87
00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:35.905
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:36.205 --> 00:05:49.783
A short report has a title, an abstract, an introduction, a method, findings, a conclusion and recommendations. I use the past simple for the method and findings and I present numbers clearly.

89
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.920
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:52.817 --> 00:05:57.884
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple for method and findings.

91
00:05:58.184 --> 00:06:02.078
Today's value is thoroughness. Do the whole job, and do it well.

92
00:06:02.378 --> 00:06:05.089
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.389 --> 00:06:08.088
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

